WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
ano toki umareta no

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
あのとき生まれたの

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
I'll softly give you my thoughts

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
watashi no omoi sotto ageru

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
私の想いそっとあげる

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
That were born at that moment

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
shinjite ite

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
信じていて

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
Please believe in them

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
deatta hi kara

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
出逢った日から

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
Since the day when we met

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
hajimete no kimochi megutteru

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
初めての気持ち巡ってる

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
For the first time, I have these feelings, and they go around

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
honto no egao hoshii nante

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
ホントの笑顔ほしいなんて

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
I want your true smile

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
anata ga oshiete kureta sorao

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
あなたが教えてくれた空を

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
I embrace the sky

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
dakishimete yume o miru

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
抱きしめて夢をみる

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
That you told me about and dream

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
tooi keredo・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
遠いけれど・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
It's faraway, but...

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
atatakai hikari no kakera

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
あたたかい光のかけら

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
The fragments of warm light

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
kizutsuita hane ni inochi o kureta no

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
傷ついた羽根に命をくれたの

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
Gave life to my wounded wings

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
fureta toki umareta

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
触れたとき生まれた

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
Born at the moment when we touched

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
tsuyoi watashi no soba ni

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
強い私のそばに

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
Next to me, who is strong

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
mamoraretai watashi ga nemutte ita no

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
守られたいわたしが眠っていたの

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
The me who wants to be protected was asleep

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
sou unmei kaerareru ne

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
そう運命変えられるね

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
That's right, destiny can be changed

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
futari no koi mezamesasete・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
ふたりの恋目覚めさせて・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
Let our love awaken...

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:29.900
{last frame of OP}

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:57.970
Kunou-san.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.260
There's some kid we don't know.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.390
Forget about him.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.470
Sure.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.810
It's only a kid, right?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.270
He probably has the wrong floor.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.400
How bothersome...

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.400
Who's there?

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.490
My name is Kurenai Shinkurou.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.910
I have a few things that I would like to discuss with the young boss, Kunou-san.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.330
And what would that be?

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.910
It concerns Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.160
What a pitiful design.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.250
Fourth Episode 「Clever Person」

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.170
You're the boss, Kunou Tadashi-san, correct?

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.300
I am Kurenai Shinkurou.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.050
Kurenai Shinkurou...

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.630
Have we met somewhere before?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:21.800
No.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.680
Look into this Kurenai Shinkurou.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.520
I've never heard of him before.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.810
We should just get rid of that kid.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.020
He seems to know about Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.150
I'd like to talk to you about the intimidation of Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.070
Intimidation?

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.070
Yes.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.450
Last week, someone had broken into the principal's house

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.240
and stole the land rights.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.370
In its place was a picture of his grand-daughter.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.460
I'm not quite sure what you're getting at.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.880
I'm referring to the threat for him to remain silent.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.880
If he reports the incident to the police, you would harm his grand-daughter-

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.510
And how exactly is this related to our office?

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.890
Related? You were the one who instructed him to, no?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.140
Please, enough joking.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.100
I've never even heard of this Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:16.940
You're trying to buy the land rights to Hanamura Kindergarten and resell it for a profit, correct?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.650
This is a copy of your orders to purchase the land rights to Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.490
There are even reports from your subordinates related to the matter.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:31.700
Also, these are the call history logs which indicate that the principal was contacted on a daily basis in order to keep him quiet.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.250
Can we resolve this in a civilized way?

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.960
Just who are you, Kurenai-kun?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.960
A dispute mediator.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.170
A dispute mediator, huh?

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.590
So, just what kind of deal are you looking for?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.510
Please return the land rights.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.560
Also, you must promise me that from now on, you will no longer concern yourself with Hanamura Kindergarten.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.270
And what's in it for us?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.520
We will dispose of the information we obtained.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.520
Is that all?

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.070
Yes.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.900
You're telling me to stop with just that?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.820
Besides, how am I supposed to believe that you'll dispose of it entirely?

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.280
Well, you'll just have to believe in us.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.790
Easier said than done.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.200
There's nothing else I can say to you.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:14.960
Kunou-san.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:15.750
What is it?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.960
There's someone here who knows him.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.710
You're not alone?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.670
Who is it?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.130
What are you doing? Let me go!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.130
I'm not anyone suspicious!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.880
I came here to see Shinkurou!

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:27.840
Murasaki!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.970
Shinkurou! You said you would protect me, so what are you doing here?

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.060
Shut up!

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.600
Your friend is a mere child?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.430
You...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.600
Were you always doing this kind of thing while I was asleep?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.150
I told you not to go outside!

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.230
Hey, damn kid,

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.150
we're not getting anywhere, so go home.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.240
No way. What about the deal?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.650
In this situation?

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.160
Do you want us to reveal the evidence to the public?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.450
Wouldn't you be troubled if we did?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.500
What are you talking about, Shinkurou?

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.420
Don't say anything.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.920
Kunou-san, I guarantee you we'll dispose of the information we've obtained.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.550
So...

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:09.630
Hey.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:20.190
Well then, please don't get involved with Hanamura Kindergarten from now on.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.400
Yeah.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.070
Hey, show them out.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:23.940
Yes.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.070
Come on, let's go home, Murasaki.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.950
That man is acting suspicious, Shinkurou!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.120
You're a liar!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.500
Don't be rude, Murasaki.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.330
Hey, dispute mediator.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:41.420
My apologies.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.500
Your face says it all.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.840
When people lie, it's shown all over their face!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.090
All right, already.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.840
I'm sorry, Kunou-san.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.840
Don't believe him, Shinkurou!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.550
Murasaki!

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.930
Don't believe him!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.310
Hurry up and leave, dispute mediator.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.260
I'm reaching my limits.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.770
Yes, we'll leave right away.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.390
She's just acting a bit strange.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.440
Don't treat me like a fool! What's so strange?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.690
I'm really sorry.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.730
Don't give in to him!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.730
Sorry.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.570
Pardon us.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:08.360
Hey!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.700
Don't be so angry.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.870
You believed in him rather than me.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.740
It's my job.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.830
Shinkurou!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.960
Shinkurou! Shinkurou!

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.340
Run, Murasaki!

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.550
Shinkurou...

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.220
Stop it! Let him go!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.100
Run away!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.720
Out of my... way!

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:42.730
Hey!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.230
Murasaki!

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.480
Murasaki!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.400
Stop!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.360
No, let go of me! Let me go!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:53.820
You should be more obedient, kid.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.120
No!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.150
His bone...

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.690
You damn punk!

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.260
That's... the Houzuki's...!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.060
Stop!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.040
This is a big job!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.830
It's an unbelievably big job where we have made enemies out of the Kuhouins!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.500
Yayoi.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.670
You don't understand how important this child is, do you?

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:29.540
I didn't explain it all properly yet.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.210
You left her behind thinking it's fine and you head off to a yakuza office?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.630
You're too careless! Just what do you think this job is?!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.340
I...

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:39.970
You're always like this!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.600
You're too careless, your thinking is too naive, and you jump to conclusions about everything too easily.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.430
Calm down, Yayoi.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.430
In the first place,

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.900
this isn't a job someone like you can handle.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.400
Things like this happen.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.490
You'll be more careful from now on, right?

00:09:58.490 --> 00:09:58.950
Yes.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.530
Okay, I'll be leaving then.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.450
I'm sorry.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.370
Benika-sama.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.460
I just can't understand.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.460
Is it because I didn't choose you?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.090
No.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.090
Then is it because I let a man handle it?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:14.880
No!

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:16.300
What is it, then?

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:22.050
Leaving myself aside, there are many other people who can protect her.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.140
So why Kurenai Shinkurou of all people?

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.730
Like I've said, it's my intuition.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.270
It's not like I doubt your intuition.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:34.520
However, you too should have realized it after today's incident.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.940
This job is impossible for Kurenai Shinkurou.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.030
I know he lacks power.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.160
I know that all too well.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.030
Then why?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.040
Let's save that discussion for another day. I'll tell you then.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.170
Today was tiring.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.420
I will stay behind.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.500
I see.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.650
Good morning, Shinkurou!

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:20.530
Are you...

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.370
...still hurt anywhere?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.370
Not at all.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.490
Anyways, I'll prepare breakfast.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.120
You can continue to rest.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.250
Oh, okay.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.500
Murasaki.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:33.630
About yesterday...

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:37.000
I caused you trouble yesterday.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.880
You got punched because I couldn't keep our promise.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.180
Well, that's...

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.720
You're angry, right?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.760
I'm not angry.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.890
It was my fault.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:53.350
I was being selfish, so it can't be helped if you're angry.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.690
I'm not angry, it was my fault.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.270
Really?

00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:59.980
Does it look like I'm lying?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:02.490
It doesn't.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.110
Right?

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.200
I'm glad you're okay.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.790
Leave breakfast to me!

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.540
You should take it easy.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.410
Sure.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.500
Is this still edible?

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.420
Morning!

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.000
Good morning.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.300
What? You didn't get enough sleep?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.260
You were watching the late-night show yesterday, weren't you?

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.510
Y-Yeah...

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.050
It was pretty funny.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.140
Gotou-chan was looking good too, huh?

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.800
Yeah, Gotou-chan.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.100
Her name is Shibiru, right?

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.980
What are you doing, Murasaki-chan?

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:39.440
Can't you tell? I'm cleaning.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.320
There's nothing in this room, though.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.490
It stinks, though.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.450
It's probably the futon that stinks.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.700
Hey.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.500
Wouldn't you normally knock before entering?

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.290
Even though it's the newspaper club's room?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:13:00.170
I'm the only member of the newspaper club, which makes this my room.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.510
And who was it that chased the other members out, again?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.670
Anyway, you came to report back, right?

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.010
Yeah.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.050
Here.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.850
Were you able to resolve it?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.310
May I tell the principal it's fine now?

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.140
Probably.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:13.270
Probably?

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.520
That's rather vague.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.640
Well, I did my job.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:20.060
We won't know if they'll stop or not, though, so we should play it safe.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.190
I see, I got it.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.320
Ah, sorry.

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:25.900
No, I'm okay.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.030
You got injured?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.570
No, I just had a bad fall.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.740
Did you get into a fight?

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.370
Yeah, kind of.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.250
This ballpen is really useful!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.000
Just the other day, a foreigner-

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.590
Maybe he was a Russian? He asked for directions.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.710
Shinkurou-san.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:44.300
Yes?

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.300
You were being careless again, weren't you?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.060
Was it a job involving Murasaki-chan?

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.640
No, it was a different one.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.400
I see.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.770
Yes.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:04.900
Let me tell you one thing as a Houzuki.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.530
You shouldn't take on jobs where you have to rely on the horn.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.700
I understand.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.870
I'll bring medicine for your wounds tomorrow.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.040
It's something my grandfather made for the inexperienced users.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.080
Inexperienced?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.170
It smells.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.460
Welcome back.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:29.970
Why have you two put futons outside of my room?

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:31.680
We're just airing them out.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.510
It's the sunniest place here.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.680
Shinkurou's futon stinks and I can't stand it.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.600
It'll be bad for my health.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.190
This... certainly does...

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.820
That's why I'm helping her.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.900
Inexperienced...

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:48.820
Inexperienced...

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.780
You certainly are inexperienced.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.410
Huh?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.410
My futon?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:02.630
It's being cleansed for the little lady's sake.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:03.710
Be grateful.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.800
That surprised me.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.300
Murasaki?

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.300
Welcome home, Shinkurou.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.800
What do you think? It's clean now, isn't it?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.810
Tamaki taught me how to, so I cleaned the room.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.310
I left your futon out in the hall to air out as well.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.980
You're letting me stay here, so I thought I should help out sometimes.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.230
Thank you.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.280
There's still something dirty!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.450
Did you wash your head?

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.540
Your assistance won't be necessary.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.380
Will you be okay?

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:53.590
Look, Shinkurou! I'm finally able to successfully wash my head by myself!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.600
That's amazing!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.020
Shampooing is easy!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:01.770
Is it cold?

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.560
I'm fine!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.560
Ah, sorry!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.270
I'm fine.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.740
Does it still hurt, Shinkurou?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.320
It was my fault, so I'm sorry.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.580
I said it's not your fault, so don't worry.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.370
Look, I have a lot of old scars too, right?

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.540
Having scars is the fate of a dispute mediator.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.540
They're like trophies to me.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.760
Are you okay? You can go up first.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:38.720
I'm fine. I'll stay in as long as you, Shinkurou.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.060
We'll get out after we count to twenty.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.310
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8...!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.640
That's too fast.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.770
We can see the stars today.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.570
I wonder if it'll be cold tomorrow morning.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.070
Hey, Shinkurou.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:54.860
Yeah?

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:59.030
Why did you become a dispute mediator?

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.830
Let's see... why <i>did </i>I become one?

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:08.210
Maybe it's because I admired Benika-san.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.250
Benika?

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.630
Yeah.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:13.260
Is Benika that good of a woman?

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:19.100
Is she a better woman than Tamaki, Yamie, Yuuno, and me?

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:24.180
Rather than admiring her as a woman, I wanted to become strong like Benika-san.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:28.520
I was really weak when I was around your age.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.400
Really?

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.230
Yeah.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:34.320
I want to hear about when you were small!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.400
It's boring.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.070
I want to know about a lot of things.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.530
I want to become stronger too!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:39.620
Stronger?

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.370
I want to be stronger!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.370
Sure.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.170
Kidnapping?

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.630
That's right.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:53.960
They bombed the airport and kidnapped the children who survived.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.340
And among them was Kurenai-san?

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.220
He lost his parents during that time.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:02.890
I'm not sure if I passed out because it was dangerous or painful.

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.720
Didn't it hurt?

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.810
It really hurt,

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.600
but then I just couldn't tell afterwards.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.690
Can that really happen?

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.440
Well, my mind just became numb.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:18.110
I wasn't afraid of dying anymore either.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:22.370
Stop! Shinkurou, Shinkurou!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.790
Shut up, you're annoying!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.880
What's up? Something funny?

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.090
Not really.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.250
You... Do you wanna die? {`a50- line split}

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.590
You... Do you wanna die? {`a50- line split}

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.050
That's fine. I don't mind dying. {hachi - you put a tlc for 331... but it makes no sense here.}

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.130
Shinkurou...?

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.760
You're real cheeky.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.390
If you want to die so badly, then I'll kill you.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.190
Stop! Please!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.650
<i>I'm</i> the one that wants to die.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.980
I know.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:57.940
Shinkurou?

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:02.450
And then, that person came.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:07.080
It was a job which couldn't be done by anyone besides those in the trade like ourselves.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.090
It happened instantly.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.140
Hurry and take the children outside!

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.560
Can you stand?

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.440
Shinkurou!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:34.610
Shinkurou?

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.480
Everything's fine now.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.740
From that day on, I followed Benika-san.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.530
I was taken under the care of Yuuno's family for a while,

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.740
and spent eight years learning the Houzuki-ryuu.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.710
It was real tough, but...

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:53.620
Thanks to it, I have the power I hold today.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.750
I see, so that's what happened.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:01.090
Benika-san then recognized me as a dispute mediator.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:03.680
Because you worked real hard.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.890
I still have a long way to go, though.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.140
Those two are quite similar.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.690
Shinkurou is the only one who can understand Murasaki's feelings.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.360
That's what I thought.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:20.440
Even so, he doesn't have the power yet.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.700
I made a promise too.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.160
It's an old story, though.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:34.540
I want the young lady, Murasaki, to be taken outside one day.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.170
How?

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.710
I'm asking you because I don't know.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.630
And what would you have her do once she's outside?

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.430
I couldn't do anything here.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:48.260
She'll meet the same fate as me if she stays.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.060
What about Renjou-sama?

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.100
He's already given up.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:55.190
I've already had three children, so it's over for me. {hachi- er check this. When the hell did murasaki have siblings? o.o;}

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.980
There's nothing more Renjou-sama can do? {hachi- check this too}

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:02.150
I don't want Murasaki to have the same experiences as I did.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.700
Renjou-sama will no longer change.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.700
Even though he loves you?

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.200
He can't abandon the Kuhouins.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.700
Is that so?

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:15.870
I see...

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.330
I am grateful to him.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:21.630
Of all the women in the Inner Sanctuary, I was the most free.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:25.840
But, I want Murasaki to know the outside world more.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.930
I want her to have a more wonderful love than me.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.600
That's a difficult request.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:33.100
Can you do it?

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:39.610
But, she died.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:43.360
She was Murasaki's real mother, right?

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:45.950
Kuhouin Souju.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:48.320
The person who couldn't win against her family's customs.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:53.330
I know that household is strange because I have worked for the Kuhouins.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:57.750
I felt I had to do it once I saw the young Murasaki.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:01.250
I know it's a lot of responsibility for Shinkurou.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:05.760
But, I thought it would benefit him as well.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:11.390
The feeling of wanting to protect someone will make you stronger.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:14.020
That's what I believe.

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.310
I'll be going to Okubo.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.140
I can take you there.

00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:19.600
I'll walk.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:21.150
You're going to Samidare Apartment, right?

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:22.730
Yes.

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:26.530
I understand the circumstances, but...

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:27.650
I'm still worried.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:29.910
Thank you.

